  "common": "usable as Source in the Common/AD Controller Box (Performance common / A/D part)",
  "part": "usable as Source in a Part Controller Box"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Marks in the PDF are a circle glyph (private-use U+F0A1, rendered as O) for available and x for not available.",
  "MIDI Data Table cross-check: Part 'Controller Set Source' (address 1p 05 bb 02) is documented as range 0-39; Common/AD 'Controller Set Source' (06 05 bb 02) is documented as range '8-15, 18-39' (Assignable Knobs 1-8, Motion Seq 1-4, Envelope Followers) even though this Control List marks all of 0-39 as usable for Common. Treat the SysEx range as the authoritative encoding limit; the discrepancy is in the source document.",
  "Part Controller Boxes: 32 per Part (address 1p 05 bb 00, bb=0-31; the address map on p.221 says 'Controller Box No. (0...32)', the parameter table on p.246 says 'bb = 0-7F Controller Box 1-32'). Common/AD Controller Boxes: 32 (06 05 bb 00, bb=0-31).",
  "Super Knob is not itself a Source number; it drives Assignable Knobs 1-8 (sources 8-15) via the Super Knob Settings / Assignable Knob Link Switches (see docs/controllers-reference.md)."
 ],
